# Vendored Guile Scheme MUST reach the compiler with LF line endings.
#
# Every file under Scheme/ is an <EmbeddedResource>, so whatever bytes are on disk at
# build time are baked into the assembly and shipped in the NuGet package. A CRLF
# checkout is therefore not a local inconvenience -- it is a broken artifact.
#
# What breaks is not obvious. The CR rides inside the multi-line format-directive
# STRING LITERALS of ice-9/format.scm, so format's directive parser runs off the end of
# its string and recurses through format-error until the process dies with an
# uncatchable stack overflow. See WHY case BINDS ITS KEY ONCE in AGENT-README.txt, which
# records the same failure shape from a different cause.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF; this only stops a Windows checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true) from expanding them on the way out, which also keeps the vendored
# files byte-identical to Guile's own so a re-sync stays a straight copy plus cmp.
*.scm text eol=lf

# The Unicode formal-name table is a deflate stream. Never touch it.
*.deflate binary
